{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-retrofit-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.79: `scale-county-retrofit` -- THC, CO, NOx, methane, NMHC, VOC and the PM2.5 total with EC, NonECPM, sulfate and aerosol water, at running and start exhaust, for the single-unit short-haul truck (52; MOVES adds every fuel of 42, 52 and 62), the combination long-haul truck (62) and the transit bus (42) in Washtenaw County at SINGLE scale, August 2020, weekday, hour 7, from the default database plus scale-county's county database WITH thirteen On-Road Retrofit programs (`inputs/washtenaw-county-retrofit.esm`, moves.rs `setup-retrofit.sql`). MOVES instantiates OnRoadRetrofitStrategy because onRoadRetrofit has rows and multiplies the finished MOVESWorkerOutput rows by each program's factor.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. The factor `rt_retrofitFactor` = 1 - sum(cumFractionRetrofit x retrofitEffectiveFraction) over the rows at the latest calendar year at or before 2020 whose model years hold the cohort's: THC running on 62 at 0.82 (model years 2000-2004, the 2012 row), 0.405 (2005-2012, the 2018 row REPLACING the 2015 row) and 0.64 (2013-2014, the 2015 row), with a 2021 row reaching nothing; CO running on 52 at 0.66 where two 2015 rows overlap (2010-2012) and SUM; NOx running on 42 at 1.1 (a negative effectiveness); the PM2.5 total on 62 at 0.3625; EC alone on 52 at 0.64; start THC on 52 at 0.75; NMHC running on 52 at 0.75. And what it does NOT reach: no child takes its parent's factor -- methane, NMHC and VOC under the THC programs, EC, NonECPM, sulfate and water under the PM2.5 program -- and the PM2.5 total does not take EC's, because the UPDATE runs after every calculator. Measured before porting against the un-retrofitted twin `scale-county-retrofit-base` (moves.rs, not wired here): every one of 15,190 nonzero cells is the twin's times the predicted factor within 7.0e-06, 2,168 cells are zero in both, and 148 (pollutant, process, fuel, source type) groups with no program are the twin's.\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to 17,358, recomputed as `rateSurvivorCount`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "control-strategy",
      "on-road-retrofit"
    ]
  },
